# Liberty City world pickups, mined from GTA III data/main.scm
#
# Every permanent pickup the source game's own main script places in the world:
# the guns lying in the street, the health, armour, adrenaline and bribes.
# Mission-owned pickups, rampages, hidden packages, save discs and Ammu-Nation
# shop stock are deliberately not here.
#
# Source opcodes, verified against the script stream rather than assumed:
#   0x0213 CREATE_PICKUP           (model, type, x, y, z)            -> handle
#   0x032B CREATE_PICKUP_WITH_AMMO (model, type, ammo, x, y, z)      -> handle
# Parameters are type-tagged: 01=int32 02=global 03=local 04=int8 05=int16
# 06=float.  In GTA III a float is a SIGNED 16-BIT FIXED-POINT value, the real number times 16 -
# not an IEEE float.
# A negative model id indexes the script's own object-name table (segment 2 of
# the SCM), which is how HEALTH / BODYARMOUR / ADRENALINE / BRIBE are named;
# a positive one indexes the game's IDE files, which is how weapons are named.
#
# Source pickup type -> San Andreas ePickupType:  14 ON_STREET_SLOW -> 15,  2 ON_STREET -> 2
#
# Columns: kind, what, pickupType, ammo, x, y, z
#   kind        `weapon` (what = a San Andreas weapon.dat name) or
#               `model`  (what = a San Andreas model id)
#   pickupType  San Andreas ePickupType (2 = ON_STREET, 15 = ON_STREET_SLOW)
#   x, y, z     Liberty City's own coordinates; the region origin is NOT applied
#
# 170 placements.
